                        <strong>Question 11 Sample 2-Point Response</strong>
                    </p>
                    <p>The map gives information about the states that were affected by the drought and the states that became known as the &#x201c;Dust Bowl.&#x201d; It also gives an idea of how large the area was and how awful it must have been because people could not easily escape from the dust and the drought. It helps the reader understand why some people, like the mother in &#x201c;Lost in the Dust,&#x201d; wanted to move far away to a place like California.</p>
